<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy

  Every list in this file is empty, and every empty list is the truth rather
  than an omission.

  The vault has no network layer at all, which is checked by a test that walks
  the source on every run rather than asserted here. It collects nothing
  because there is nowhere for anything to go. It tracks nothing because there
  is no identifier to track with and no request to carry one.

  The API list is empty because the app calls none of the required-reason APIs.
  No user defaults, no file timestamps, no disk space, no boot time, no
  keyboard list. Checked, not assumed: test/shipping.test.ts greps the Swift
  for each of those families and fails if one appears without a matching
  declaration here.

  If any of that stops being true, this file is wrong and the test is what
  will say so. An accurate manifest is a promise to somebody reading the App
  Store listing, and it is the cheapest promise in the product to keep.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
    <false/>
    <key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
    <array/>
    <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
    <array/>
    <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
    <array/>
</dict>
</plist>
